    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d493-a4">

                <pb facs="0813" n="679" xml:id="pg679"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Sewall to Mr.
                            Becker.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate-General of the United States of America</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Apia Samoa</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1888-02-13"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 13, 1888</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to our correspondence <hi
                        rendition="#italic">re</hi> the pilot station, I have the honor to inform
                    you that the title to the land in question is now vested in myself, and that I
                    decline to entertain any of the propositions made in your letter of 31st of
                    January.</p>
                <p>I respectfully request that you notify the present occupant, who I understand is
                    a German subject, to remove forthwith.</p>
                <p>An early acknowledgment of this will oblige me.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Harold Marsh
                                Sewall</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Consul-General.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
